# Renew the Salla credential BEFORE it expires (CHANGELOG §29, condition 4).
#
# The credential expired on 2026-07-29 with no path to renew it and nobody was
# told for nine days; the first symptom was paid orders that provisioned
# nothing. This unit is the «مؤقّت يملك سببه» that closes it.
#
# Type=oneshot with OnFailure=, exactly like career-backup.service and
# career-engine-nightly.service: a scheduled job that exits non-zero is a job
# that did not do its work, and career-alert@ puts that fact on the operator's
# phone once, deduplicated. The ACTIONABLE sentence — «reinstall the app on
# your store» — comes from the script's own admin message, which escalates by
# tier instead of repeating; the two are deliberately different messages,
# because «the refresh job failed» and «the credential is about to die and
# only you can fix it» need different words and different frequencies.
#
# EnvironmentFile carries SALLA_CLIENT_ID / SALLA_CLIENT_SECRET and the
# Telegram admin credentials. No DB_HOST/REDIS_HOST override ride-along is
# needed here (unlike career-engine-nightly.service): this job touches neither
# Postgres nor Redis — it reads the credential store, calls one HTTPS endpoint
# and writes the credential file back through it.
#
# NOT installed by anyone but Fahad: this file is the deliverable, and the
# `cp` + `daemon-reload` + `enable --now` is his gated step (scripts/gate.sh
# --host tells him whether the machine is running what this repository says).
[Unit]
Description=Refresh the Salla OAuth credential before it expires
Wants=network-online.target
After=network-online.target
OnFailure=career-alert@%n.service

[Service]
Type=oneshot
WorkingDirectory=/root/career
EnvironmentFile=/root/career/.env.staging
ExecStart=/root/career/.venv/bin/python /root/career/scripts/refresh_salla_token.py
# The script takes its own single-flight lock (a second refresh presenting the
# same single-use token is how Salla's OAuth server is made to revoke
# everything), so a run that overlaps its predecessor exits without asking.
# This is the outer belt: a hung HTTPS call cannot pile runs up across days.
TimeoutStartSec=120
